    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Trevor Story** (73.47), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against shaky arms in Gallen and Johnson. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains our primary offensive threat, fueled by an excellent 4.94 xERA matchup and a clear platoon advantage that bolsters his profile in our 5x5 build. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (68.53) and **James Wood** (67.81) stand out as high-ceiling plays; **James Wood** brings elite xwOBA metrics to the table, and his lead-off spot against Buehler provides the necessary volume to capitalize on his speed, which is a vital commodity given our focus on stealing bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **Cole Young** (51.76) on the bench. While **Cole Young** shows potential, he narrowly missed the cut behind the superior efficiency of **Josh Naylor** (62.78) and **Max Muncy** (59.43). **Max Muncy** specifically gets a boost despite facing a righty, as his matchup against Fisher and the potential for a slow delivery from the mound keeps his SB-weighted efficiency just above the threshold to displace the reserves. We are also monitoring **Seiya Suzuki** (45.59) closely; his score is dragged down by a poor matchup against Henderson, yet he remains in the lineup due to the lack of viable speed threats on the bench today, as **Corbin Carroll** is out of the lineup and our secondary options like **Austin Riley** and **Isaac Paredes** are facing tougher pitching conditions.\n\nRisk management remains a priority as we navigate a slate where several of our hitters are forced into unfavorable platoon spots. **Jose Caballero** (55.35) carries the highest variance today, with his score suppressed by his #9 spot in the lineup, yet we are keeping him active strictly to chase SB potential. While we are comfortable with our starters, keep an eye on **Griffin Conine**; he faces an elite catcher's arm (1.87s pop time) which mitigates some of his aggressive base-running upside. With game caps nearing, we are prioritizing efficiency over raw totals, ensuring that peripheral assets like **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Edwin Arroyo** stay in reserve unless a late lineup change forces a pivot.",
